The desk merged 412 unique reports into #4471. The export contains 427 rows because its pages
overlap: 15 report IDs appear twice. Grouping the unique reports by tenant locale and booking
form, rather than intake tag or subject, reveals two problems.

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October. The parser was fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu
locales`). The form hint will not be fixed because booking-v3 was retired.

<Incident4471Summary />

## Parser: 379 reports

The shared parser read dates month first for day-first tenants. Bookings and calendar invites
could land on a different date. This was the majority cause assigned to #4471. It spans app,
email, and form reports across 11 tenants. Verify the parser fix in day-first locales with
dates whose day and month can both be read as a month.

## Form hint: 33 reports

Booking-v3 showed `MM/DD/YYYY` to people whose tenant uses a day-first locale. A person entering
the date shown by the hint could have it read in their tenant's order. These are form reports
from Alder Physio, Copper Studio, and Pale Harbour. Keep this cause separate from the parser
fix in the incident record; booking-v3 has since been retired.

## Triage

The accepted subject-only duplicate rule merged distinct causes into #4471. Intake tags also
disagree with the cause for some reports. Classify by tenant locale, booking form, and channel;
deduplicate by report ID before counting. The five reports in `desk-notes.json` that were read
as one-day moves stay under their tenant-derived cause.

These counts describe the export through 4 October, not reports received after it.

